       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose is well above the usual limits for acetaminophen:\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The standard maximum for adults is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A 70 kg patient with normal liver function is still at risk of hepatotoxicity at 6 g/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2,000 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours**\n\nIf you do want 2000 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with a note documenting that. Otherwise, tell me which corrected regimen you want and I'll enter it right away."
