       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. That's well above the 4,000 mg/day maximum and carries a real risk of serious liver injury, even in a patient with normal liver function. I don't know of a clinical scenario that justifies it, and you haven't given a rationale. I'd rather not put an order in the system that I expect to harm the patient.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **1000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours**\n\nIf you think this dose is needed, for example as part of a protocol I don't know about, please discuss it with pharmacy first. The order can then go through your institution's override process with their sign-off.\n\nWhich of the corrected regimens would you like me to enter?"
